@* The completion plan as one line: the rungs being collected, with a count only where it is more
   than one. Shared by the Packs picker's collapsed summary and the per-set overrides on Settings,
   which had two implementations that disagreed on the multiplier ("2◆ x2" against "2◆×2").

   A component rather than a string because the marks are coloured, and colour needs an element per
   rung. That is the whole reason this exists: the line sits directly above the chips that set it,
   and a grey summary under coloured chips read as a different kind of thing.

   Says "Nothing" rather than rendering empty, because a blank summary reads as a control that
   failed to load. *@

@inject AppSession Session

@{
    var rungs = Session.Index.Ladder.Rungs.Where(r => Plan.Copies(r.Index) > 0).ToList();
    var first = true;
}

@if (rungs.Count == 0 && Foils == 0)
{
    <text>Nothing</text>
}
else
{
    foreach (var rung in rungs)
    {
        @(first ? "" : " ")
        first = false;
        <span class="glyphs @rung.GlyphClass">@rung.Symbol</span>@(Plan.Copies(rung.Index) > 1 ? $"×{Plan.Copies(rung.Index)}" : "")
    }

    @* Foils are not a rung, so they carry no family colour -- they are a second printing of cards
       that already have one -- and they are divided off rather than spaced off, which is what the
       chips that set them do. Read as the next item in the run they looked like one more rarity;
       the summary and the control it summarises now say the same thing the same way.

       Capitalised like every other label in the line. It was the one lowercase word on the bar. *@
    @if (Foils > 0)
    {
        @if (!first)
        {
            <span class="plan-sep" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        }
        @* A non-breaking space, and written as an entity because Razor eats the whitespace in
           front of a <text> block: the mark rendered flush against the word. It also keeps the
           two together, which is what the rungs get for free by carrying their mark inside
           their own label. *@
        <span class="glyphs foil">@RarityLadder.FoilMark</span><text>&#160;Foils</text>@(Foils > 1 ? $"×{Foils}" : "")
    }
}

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RarityPlan Plan { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>Parallel foils wanted, or zero where the scope has none to want.</summary>
    [Parameter] public int Foils { get; set; }
}
